      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "Best Email Marketing Platform to Grow Your Business | Mailchimp",
      "pageDescription": "Are you exploring the best email marketing platforms? See how Mailchimp’s email marketing platform can help grow your business with our best-in-class tools.",
      "evidenceText": "Best Email Marketing Platform to Grow Your Business | Mailchimp Skip to main content Join Mailchimp with a free 14-day trial or save 15% off on 10,000+ contacts. Start today. EMAIL MARKETING PLATFORM Convert more customers with a powerful and intuitive platform Create personalized emails, target precisely with behavior-based automations and segments, and optimize with real-time reporting. Enter email address Start with a free 14-day trial and send your first email today. Terms apply.† Email marketing, powered by AI — your partner for converting more customers The #1 AI-powered email marketing and automations platform* that recommends ways to get more opens, clicks, and sales. Up to 30x ROI seen by Mailchimp users* >99% deliverability rate for email (average) 11M+ Users of Mailchimp globally 50+ behavior-based triggers for personalization Personalize your marketing at scale Fuel e-commerce growth with new automations Proactively reach customers when they're ready to buy or churn with predictive automations that drive revenue. Learn about new triggers Save time with templates just for e-commerce Get a head start on your next e-mail with professionally-designed templates built specifically to support e-commerce growth. Explore the template gallery Reach more customers with less effort Mailchimp’s automations help you engage your audience at the right time, with the right message, and without any manual intervention. Explore automations Reach more customers - Automations Image showcasing an abstract view of Mailchimp's app interface highlighting the advanced segmentation feature. Generate ROI with advanced segmentation Our powerful segmentation logic and filters help you use relevant and timely communication to target the customers most likely to purchase. Explore segmentation Mailchimp’s SMS platform is more powerful than ever We’re introducing new enhancements to our SMS marketing tools all the time—so you can keep growing and outpacing the competition. Explore SMS features Create effective marketing campaigns in minutes with AI-powered design tools Let AI help you write the first draft Intuit Assist helps you quickly craft relevant content like headlines and body copy. It can even create fully built emails—all you need to do is review, edit, and publish. Explore generative AI Image of an abstract view of an email interface, where the headline is being actively edited using Mailchimp's generative AI builder feature. The AI suggests creative and engaging headlines and also offers prompt suggestions such as a sales announcement. Image of an abstracted view of Mailchimp's product recommendations tool in the Email Builder. Drive sales with AI-powered product recommendations Use preset feeds like best sellers or new arrivals to send personalized emails with dynamic recommendations based on your customer interactions. Explore dynamic product recommendations Create stunning emails faster by choosing from 130+ high-quality templates Pick and personalize the design that’s just right Choose a template that fits your industry and unique business goals to see the difference a great layout can make. Explore templates Image of a carousel showing various email template options from Mailchimp's Email Template Library. Users can select from a range of professionally designed templates tailored for different types of email campaigns and business needs. Make smarter decisions based on personalized benchmarking Stay connected to the apps and services you love Make Mailchimp your single source of truth for marketing activities. We offer 300+ integrations so you have everything you need in a single location. Explore 300+ Integrations Track, analyze, and optimize your impact—so you can sell more See what's working and make informed decisions with an omni-channel dashboard, audience analytics, testing, and more. Explore Reporting and Analytics Get up and running easily with personalized onboarding services Get guided support from an onboarding specialist—available with a Standard or Premium plan. Learn more To watch this video, you need to accept Performance and Functionality Cookies . For more info, check our cookie policy . We're sorry. Due to a technical issue, the video is currently unable to load. Please try again later. Onboarding services video We offer expert 24/7 customer service Our customer service team is always available and ready to support you if you ever need help. See our support offerings FAQs What is email marketing software? Email marketing software is a tool that helps businesses send emails to customers and prospects at scale. Instead of manually typing out individual messages, you can create, design, and send professional campaigns to hundreds or thousands of people at once. These platforms typically include templates, automation features, analytics, and tools to help you organize your contacts. Whether you're announcing a sale, sharing company news, or nurturing leads, email marketing software streamlines the entire process. What does an email marketing platform do? An email marketing platform handles everything from designing your emails to tracking how well they perform. You can build campaigns using drag-and-drop editors, personalize messages for different audience segments, and schedule sends for optimal timing. Most SMS and email marketing platforms also let you automate repetitive tasks like welcome emails or birthday messages. Beyond sending, the best email marketing platforms provide insights into open rates, click-throughs, and conversions so you can see what's working and what needs adjustment. Basically, it takes the heavy lifting out of staying connected with your audience. How effective is email marketing? Many people ask the question, \" Is email marketing dead? \" The simple answer is that it's very much alive and well. Email marketing is one of the most effective digital marketing channels available. It delivers a strong return on investment because you're reaching people who have already shown an interest in your brand by signing up. With email marketing solutions like Mailchimp, you can target specific groups with personalized content, which drives higher engagement. The benefits of email marketing are direct communication, measurability, and the ability to scale your efforts without proportionally increasing costs. What are the four types of email marketing campaigns? There are many types of email marketing campaigns. However, there are four principal types of marketing emails, which include: Promotional emails: Promotional emails advertise a company’s products or services, often by promoting sales, discounts, seasonal events, company events, and so on. Product update emails: These emails inform customers about new or updated products. Digital newsletters: Digital newsletters are regularly sent to a company’s email list to inform customers of company or industry updates by providing interesting articles or relevant news. Transactional emails: These emails are typically triggered by a customer action. For example, if a customer buys a product, they may receive a confirmation email or a follow-up email that asks for their feedback. How can I optimize email marketing campaigns? Optimizing your campaigns comes down to testing what works and refining based on results. Your subject lines determine whether someone opens your message, so keep them short, relevant, and intriguing without being clickbait-y. Segment your audience so you're sending the right content to the right people — a one-size-fits-all approach rarely works well. Test different send times, layouts, and calls to action to see what resonates. Make sure your emails look good on mobile devices since most people read on their phones. Also, clean your list regularly by removing inactive subscribers to maintain strong deliverability. If you need inspiration, check out these email campaign examples to spark ideas. What makes Mailchimp the best email marketing platform for small, new e-commerce websites? Mailchimp is the best email marketing platform because it's built to help small and medium-sized businesses grow without needing a huge team or technical expertise. You get access to over 130 pre-built email templates designed for e-commerce and retail, so you don't need coding skills to create professional campaigns. Features like dynamic content let you personalize messages automatically, while powerful customer segmentation ensures you're targeting the right shoppers with relevant offers. Abandoned cart emails help recover lost sales by reminding customers about items they've left behind. Mailchimp's user-friendly design tools mean you can start selling and engaging customers right away, even if you're just learning email marketing basics . Is Mailchimp's email marketing platform reliable? Can it handle high-volume sends? Absolutely. Mailchimp's infrastructure powers millions of emails every day for over 11 million customers globally. The platform maintains an average delivery rate for transactional and marketing emails above 99%, which means your messages actually reach inboxes instead of getting lost or marked as spam. Mailchimp customers have sent more than 3.1 billion emails using AI-generated content, proving our system can handle serious volume. Whether you're sending emails to a few hundred subscribers or scaling up to hundreds of thousands, you can count on fast, secure delivery with proven deliverability rates. What makes Mailchimp the best email marketing service for sending sales emails? Sales teams need ways to stay connected with prospects and clients. Mailchimp lets you send professional, branded emails that look polished and build trust with recipients. You can use segmentation and automations to tailor messages to specific audiences, ensuring your outreach feels relevant rather than generic. Mailchimp offers tons of email and form templates designed for different marketing and sales scenarios and business types. Meanwhile, advanced reporting shows you exactly who opened, clicked, or engaged with your emails, so your team knows which leads to follow up with and when. Is Mailchimp a good email marketing platform when managing multiple Shopify stores? Yes. Mailchimp is actually ideal for this situation. We offer over 300 integrations, making it easier to connect your various data sources. You can integrate multiple Shopify stores and other leading e-commerce platforms with one Mailchimp account. With Mailchimp acting as a central hub, you can more easily manage audiences, campaigns, and reports across different shops. The Shopify integration specifically helps unlock the power of your store data by letting you set up automations like welcome series and abandoned cart sequences using information directly from your store. With more e-commerce data flowing into Mailchimp, you get stronger personalization, more automation opportunities, and better overall results. Does Mailchimp's email marketing platform have automation and segmentation? Absolutely. You can set up automated journeys for all kinds of scenarios, including welcome emails when someone subscribes, abandoned cart reminders, and re-engagement campaigns for inactive customers, and more. Advanced segmentation lets you target customers based on their behaviors, purchase history, and preferences, ensuring your messages reach the right people at the right time. This combination of automation and segmentation is what makes modern email marketing strategies so powerful. You're not just blasting the same message to everyone — you're creating personalized experiences that drive better engagement and conversions. Will Mailchimp's email marketing platform integrate well with my CRM? Yes. Mailchimp's email marketing services connect with hundreds of apps, including popular CRMs, so your customer data stays in sync across platforms. That way, you can use the insights from your CRM to personalize campaigns and nurture leads more effectively. When your tools can communicate, you get a complete picture of each customer's journey, which helps you send more relevant, timely messages. The integration options make Mailchimp flexible enough to fit into whatever tech stack you're already using. Is Mailchimp's email marketing software easy to use? Mailchimp is designed for all levels of marketers, whether you're a beginner or an expert. The intuitive drag-and-drop editor, pre-built templates, and guided steps mean you can create professional and effective campaigns quickly, even if you've never sent a marketing email before. As you get more comfortable, you still have the flexibility to customize your email marketing strategy as your business grows. The platform is also easy to use for teams. If you have multiple users on your account, you can edit collaboratively in the email builder, see which team members are working on an email, send tests to request feedback, and leave comments. Plus, customers can always access human assistance services and 24/7 chat support depending on their plan. Here's a free marketing features overview to help you get started with the essentials and see what's possible. How can I start email marketing? Email marketing can serve as a cornerstone of any company’s digital marketing strategy. If you don’t already have an email marketing strategy in place or you’re interested in improving your company’s email marketing campaigns, check out Mailchimp. Gain access to free email marketing tools when you create an account with Mailchimp. With our email marketing services, you can quickly and easily organize your audience, segment customers, write and design emails, set timing preferences and triggers, and evaluate your performance. Need to hire a helping hand? We got you. From a quick template design to full-service campaign management, our global community of 850+ trusted experts does it all. Explore Mailchimp Experts Email marketing topics Email Segmentation Tools: Segment Your List to Drive Conversions Use Mailchimp's email segmentation tools to segment subscribers by demographics, behavior, or interests. Email A/B Testing Tools: Test Subject Lines, Content, Send Times, and more. See how Mailchimp's A/B testing features can improve your email marketing and drive more conversions. Email Automation Tools: Automate Marketing to Reach Customers on Time See how Mailchimp's email automation tools can automate marketing to reach more customers on time. Email Deliverability: Reach More Inboxes with 99%+ Delivery Rate See how Mailchimp's email deliverability ensures your messages land in inboxes, not spam. Millions of users trust us with their email marketing. You can too. Get started *Disclaimers 58% Higher Click Rate : Based on US users who sent both email and SMS campaigns compared to users who sent only email campaigns from 8/1/23 to 5/14/24. 16x SMS ROI : Based on U.S. SMS users’ e-commerce revenue attributable to SMS campaigns within 90 days of launch during September 2023 through April 2024. 30X ROI : Based on all e-commerce revenue attributable to paid plan users’ Mailchimp campaigns from August 2024 - August 2025. ROI calculation requires an e-commerce store that is connected to a Mailchimp account. Results vary. SMS Marketing: SMS is available as an add-on to US, UK, Canada, or Australia paid plans only. Application and agreement to terms is required before purchasing credits. Messages can only be delivered to contacts in the country selected. Australia messaging available only for contacts with +61 country code. SMS credits are added to your account after purchase and approval. Credits are issued monthly and unused credits expire and do not roll over. MMS only available for Standard and Premium plans sending to US or Canada contacts. Pricing varies. See terms for details. Intuit Assist: Intuit Assist functionality (beta) is available to certain users with Premium, Standard and Legacy plans in select countries in English only. Access to Intuit Assist is available at no additional cost at this time. Pricing, terms, conditions, special features and service options are subject to change without notice. Availability of features and functionality varies by plan type. Features may be broadly available soon but represents no obligation and should not be relied on in making a purchasing decision. For details, please view Mailchimp’s various plans and pricing. Personalized onboarding: Onboarding services differ per plan and are available for new or upgraded users with a Standard or Premium plan for the first 90 days after account creation or upgrade. Onboarding services are currently offered in English, Spanish and Portuguese for Premium plans, and in English for Standard plans. Popup forms (beta): Very limited availability to new and existing Mailchimp users and on web browsers only. Features may be more broadly available soon, but represents no obligation and should not be relied on in making a purchasing decision. Availability of features and functionality varies by plan type. For details, view plans and pricing . 2x More Revenue with Predictive Segments: Standard and Premium users saw 2x more revenue (266%) on average for their connected ecommerce stores using predictive segmented emails versus non-predictive segmented emails for Jan 2023 - Dec 2024 period. Predictive segments available on Standard or Premium plans only. #1 AI-powered email marketing platform: Based on May 2025 publicly available data on number of customers of competitors that also advertise using AI to enhance their email marketing and automation products and services. Availability of features and functionality varies by plan type. For details, view plans and pricing. † Free Trial Terms : The first fourteen (14) days of subscription to Mailchimp Standard or Essentials (as applicable, each, a “monthly plan”), starting from the date of enrollment, is free (“Free Trial”). Valid payment information must be provided at the time of enrollment. You will be notified via e-mail of the approaching expiration of your Free Trial prior to the expiration date. To be eligible for the free trial offer, you must be a new Mailchimp customer or an existing Free Marketing Plan customer with an account created within the last 90 days in select countries and sign up for a Standard or Essentials plan using the \"Start Free Trial\" option (or similar wording). Offer is limited to one per Mailchimp account and cannot be combined with other Mailchimp offers and offers are not eligible to be applied consecutively. Offer is available for a limited time only and does not apply to add-on fees or one-time fees, including but not limited to transactional email (fka Mandrill) charges, SMS Marketing, Website plans, pay as you go credits, or Google ads. Once the Trial Period ends, you will be charged on a monthly or annual basis, as applicable, at the then-current rate for the paid marketing plan you have selected based on your contacts and emails sends until you cancel, change to a different paid monthly or annual marketing plan, or change to a Free Marketing Plan. If you purchase an annual Paid Marketing Plan while on a free trial, your free trial will immediately terminate upon purchase. See full offer terms. Terms, conditions, pricing, special features, and service and support options subject to change without notice. Related Links: Powerful marketing features that help your business grow faster Win customers with the #1 email marketing and automations platform* We’ve got your back—and the FREE email marketing tools to prove it. Products Why Mailchimp? Product Updates Email Marketing Transactional Email How We Compare GDPR Compliance Security Status Mobile App Resources Marketing Library Free Marketing Tools Marketing Glossary Integrations Directory Community Agencies & Freelancers Developers Events Company Our Story Newsroom Give Where You Live Careers Accessibility Help Contact Us Hire an Expert Help Center Talk to 