      "title": "🔴 Sources say Trump Jr. discussed deals with Kremlin-linked businessman",
      "url": "https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/donald-trump-jr-discussed-deals-with-russian-businessman-close-to-putins-personal-security-chief-two-sources-say",
      "category": "uncategorized",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-16T16:53:40.266Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/donald-trump-jr-discussed-deals-with-russian-businessman-close-to-putins-personal-security-chief-two-sources-say",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
      "pageTitle": "Donald Trump Jr. Discussed Deals With Russian Businessman Close to Putin&rsquo;s Personal Security Chief, Two Sources Say",
      "pageDescription": "Trump Jr. and Umar Kremlev have been widely reported as friends, with the controversial businessman even paying for Trump Jr.&rsquo;s wedding. But according to two independent sources, the two men sat down in Kazakhstan to talk business.",
      "evidenceText": "Donald Trump Jr. Discussed Deals With Russian Businessman Close to Putin&rsquo;s Personal Security Chief, Two Sources Say | OCCRP Power and Influence • United States Donald Trump Jr. Discussed Deals With Russian Businessman Close to Putin’s Personal Security Chief, Two Sources Say Trump Jr. and Umar Kremlev have been widely reported as friends, with the controversial businessman even paying for Trump Jr.’s wedding. But according to two independent sources, the two men sat down in Kazakhstan to talk business. Banner: James O’Brien/OCCRP Reported by Roman Anin Important Stories Also published by our partner Important Stories (Russia, in Russian) November 4, 2026 | 4 min read Share Article &times; Aa Text Settings &times; Text Size Small Medium Large Line Spacing Compact Normal Spacious Donald Trump Jr. makes no secret of his relationship with Kremlin-linked businessman Umar Kremlev. In 2025, the two men appeared together on stage in Istanbul at a meeting of the International Boxing Association, of which Kremlev is president. “I am proud to call Umar not only a leader but a friend,” Trump Jr. said. And earlier this year, after ProPublica revealed that Kremlev had rented out a private island for Trump Jr.’s wedding, his new wife posted on Instagram that this had been “an extraordinarily generous” gift from “our dear friend Umar.” But now, as reported by OCCRP’s Russian partner Important Stories , there may be more than friendship on the agenda. Two sources independently told the outlet’s reporters that Kremlev told them he and Trump Jr. had met in Kazakhstan to discuss business deals earlier this year. Credit: Screenshot/iba.sport/International Boxing Association Umar Kremlev (left) and Donald Trump Jr. (right) speak at a meeting of the International Boxing Association in Istanbul, Turkey, on September 29, 2025. Credit: Screenshot/iba.sport/International Boxing Association Umar Kremlev (left) and Donald Trump Jr. (right) speak at a meeting of the International Boxing Association in Istanbul, Turkey, on September 29, 2025. Kremlev referred to those encounters as “business meetings,” they said. Both sources were quoted anonymously to ensure their safety. A spokesperson for Donald Trump Jr. denied these claims, telling Important Stories that, despite being “personal friends,” the two men “have never entered into any business deals with each other and have no plans to do so.” Kremlev did not respond to questions, and an assistant said she could provide no comment. The relationship between the U.S. president’s son and Kremlev is significant because the latter is close to Russian circles of power. His name appeared on a leaked list of officials, state-company executives, and businesspeople whose properties had been hidden on the official government real estate registry. Others on that list included the prime minister, the interior minister, and the head of the state oil giant Rosneft. The legal basis for the concealment, for Kremlev or the others, is not publicly known. The sources who spoke with Important Stories, both of whom know Kremlev, also said that he travels in official Rosgvardia vehicles accompanied by armed guards, a level of protection granted to high-ranking officials or other individuals designated by Putin. Credit: KREMLIN/AFP President Vladimir Putin awards Umar Kremlev the Order of Friendship on April 22, 2026 as part of a ceremony honoring Russian world boxing champions. Credit: KREMLIN/AFP President Vladimir Putin awards Umar Kremlev the Order of Friendship on April 22, 2026 as part of a ceremony honoring Russian world boxing champions. In 2024, the independent Russian outlet Proekt reported that Kremlev owes his business empire to the influence of a powerful friend — the head of Putin’s presidential security service. He has not publicly responded to this reporting, and he did not respond to OCCRP’s requests for comment about it. The outlet reported that he was born Umar Lutfulloyev in Tajikistan, but moved to Russia at a young age, and that he was convicted of extortion in 2004 and battery in 2007 before changing his last name to Kremlev in 2010. This reporting is confirmed by leaked law enforcement databases. (His press office told ProPublica that “Mr. Kremlev has a completely clean legal record.”) According to Proekt, two of Kremlev’s acquaintances said that he was introduced to Putin’s top personal security official, Alexei Rubezhnoi, by the head of the pro-Kremlin Night Wolves motorcycle club. Reporters could not independently verify this, but Instagram photos show the two men boxing and celebrating holidays together. Credit: Screenshot/Instagram/umar_kremlev In an Instagram post, Kremlev (right) poses with Rubezhnoi (left) on his birthday in 2021. Credit: Screenshot/Instagram/umar_kremlev In an Instagram post, Kremlev (right) poses with Rubezhnoi (left) on his birthday in 2021. Kremlev’s star began to rise. In 2017, Rubezhnoi was named board chairman of Russia’s boxing federation — and immediately advanced Kremlev for the position of general secretary. Kremlev also bought the country's largest car dealership from the state, which had seized it from its previous owner. Several people Proekt described as Kremlev’s proxies, including a personal assistant and an advisor, also acquired stakes in three of Russia’s leading sports betting companies. And in 2021, Kremlev and a boxing organization he founded acquired a combined 51-percent stake in TsUPIS, a major betting-payments operator. The same year, Putin designated TsUPIS as Russia's exclusive payments platform for sports betting. Important Stories’ sources did not provide any further details on what Kremlev and Trump Jr. may have discussed in Kazakhstan, but the U.S. president’s son already has business interests in the country. As the Financial Times reported earlier this year, he and his brother Eric Trump acquired a stake in a construction company called Skyline Builders in 2025. That company then acquired 20 percent of Kaz Resources, a company created to mine one of the world’s largest tungsten deposits in the country’s central Karaganda region. Six days later, the U.S. and Kazakh governments announced an agreement to grant a company in the Kaz Resources investment group access to the deposits. Two U.S. government agencies have also expressed interest in providing up to $1.6 billion in federal financing for the project. November 4, 2026 Share Article: Reported by Roman Anin Important Stories Also published by our partner Important Stories (Russia, in Russian) Related Articles 4 months ago Businessman Who Allegedly Posed as CIA Agent Wooed Indonesian President and His Brother Power and Influence Indonesia 6 months ago US Securities Regulator Moves to Settle Adani Civil Case Power and Influence United States 9 years ago Paradise Papers Top Kazakhstani Official Holds Stake in Secretive Transportation Empire Enablers Russia 4 months ago Businessman Who Allegedly Posed as CIA Agent Wooed Indonesian President and His Brother Power and Influence Indonesia 6 months ago US Securities Regulator Moves to Settle Adani Civil Case Power and Influence United States 9 years ago Paradise Papers Top Kazakhstani Official Holds Stake in Secretive Transportation Empire Enablers Russia Help us improve the website! Click below to give us input. It’ll only take 5 minutes. 👉 Help OCCRP Don't show this anymore",
