BERS A dead homeless man was known as ‘Box Mike’ — until a global search revealed his true identity FOR SUBSCRIBERS Iran-backed Houthis tighten siege on strategic Yemen city, sparking famine fears FOR SUBSCRIBERS ‘Yalta 2.0’: Why some are wary of a Trump-Putin-Xi summit FOR SUBSCRIBERS The rise and fall of Russell Brand: From controversial comedian to convicted rapist FOR SUBSCRIBERS Democrats say Trump family businesses top upcoming investigations FOR SUBSCRIBERS What does the blue wave mean for trans rights? It’s complicated FOR SUBSCRIBERS For Victoria’s Secret, inclusivity has become sexy — and a solid business strategy FOR SUBSCRIBERS How Nvidia ‘honeypot’ spy scandal could backfire on China Slide 1 of 1 Perez was a technical assistant to the president who had served as a teleprompter operator for Trump since 2016. The CFTC cited what it called Perez’s “exemplary cooperation” in the case when announcing the fine and penalties Friday. Then-White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt in July called the online trades a breach of ethics and “deeply unfortunate and frankly a disgrace.” Perez was placed on leave in July and Leavitt said at the time that “this individual will no longer be here.” Share Add NBC News to Google Phil Helsel Phil Helsel is a reporter for NBC News. Steve Kopack contributed .",
